From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anh Mac <anhmac@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:47:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/48] [Extensions] Update controlled content settings when
 extension state change

Previously, ContentSettingsService only updated extension-controlled
content settings in ContentSettingsStore via
ExtensionPrefsObserver::OnExtensionStateChanged(), which is triggered
solely by changes to extension disable reasons [1]. Because extensions
blocklisted for malware (BLOCKLISTED_MALWARE) are unloaded without
adding a disable reason, their controlled content settings remained
active when blocklisted at runtime.

This change ensures extension-controlled content settings are removed
when an extension is loaded/unloaded for any reason (blocklisted,
disabled, etc.):
- Make `ContentSettingsService` observe `ExtensionRegistry` and override
  `OnExtensionLoaded()` and `OnExtensionUnloaded()` to update the
  extension's state in `ContentSettingsStore`. When an extension's active
  state changes at runtime, `ExtensionRegistrar` triggers
  `ExtensionRegistry::TriggerOnUnloaded` / `TriggerOnLoaded`, updating
  `ContentSettingsStore` accordingly.
- Add a browser test in `content_settings_apitest.cc`
  (`ExtensionContentSettingsApiTest.SettingsRemovedOnBlocklist`)
  verifying that extension-controlled content settings are reset to
  default when the extension is blocklisted.

[1]
https://source.corp.google.com/h/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:extensions/browser/extension_prefs.cc;l=2027;drc=7a77a41779ef2069a6eba534616eb61be0939d6b

